      "line_end": 128,
      "text": "Long-term memory is designed to handle timelines. When retrieving information, the associated timeline allows an LLM to see when similar points were made, identify if a point was later overturned, and determine which version of the information is current and should be adopted.",
      "completeness": "complete",
